# Build context = apps/api (used when the API is built standalone — e.g.
# `docker build -f Dockerfile apps/api`). The production image in this repo is
# normally built with the repo ROOT as context (see Dockerfile + root
# .dockerignore); this file applies whenever apps/api is the context.
#
# Dev dependencies are reinstalled inside the image (apps/api/Dockerfile keeps
# node_modules from the builder stage), so local installs must not leak in.

# dependencies / build output
node_modules
dist
coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets / env — NEVER copy into an image
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example

# local uploads + logs
.data
*.log
**/*.log